A person is guilty of a violation of this section when, without legal justification, he discharges the following firearms or explosives under the following circumstances:
(1) Discharge of center fire rifles and pistols and shotguns with slugs within 1,500 feet of a dwelling without the permission of the inhabitant;
(2) Discharge of rim fire rifles and pistols and shotguns with buckshot within 300 feet of a public highway, road, or street, or within 1,000 feet of a dwelling without the permission of the inhabitant;
(3) Discharge of shotguns with birdshot within 150 feet of a public highway, road, or street, or within 300 feet of a dwelling without the permission of the inhabitant.
(Ord. of 4-4-2002(2), § 1(14-6))
